{"base_rate":0.3652530779753762,"brier":0.13483652530779752,"bss":0.41841517741831336,"bss_hi":0.520255414580519,"bss_lo":0.29800916663558935,"chart":{"base":[377.7,130.4],"fp":[203.0,190.5],"lead":"62,261.8 272,249.8 482,238.1 692,230","note":{"base":"skill 0.42 — higher than 79% of cities","fp":"low end -1pp, high end +20pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 67% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 1%; promised 100% → rained 91%"},"rel":"72.3,463 372.7,340 617.9,212.2 691.7,70.9"},"country":"BD","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.11889192886456906,"ess":193.886404110289,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Chattogram</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Chattogram rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>91%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(2%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 731 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 7.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.42, ranked 45 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(16&ndash;103) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>292</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>64%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>58%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>60%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>91%</b></td><td class='num'>152</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Chattogram</b> <span class=\"muted\">Bangladesh</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;37% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 37% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.42</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>16&ndash;103\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>731 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Chattogram &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Chattogram\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"63.80705479452055,370.7808219178082 180.6876712328767,217.45205479452056 285.9061971830985,105.15492957746477 346.6709090909091,51.09090909090912 390.66805194805187,22.727272727272748 411.83697368421053,18.0 411.83697368421053,20.39473684210526 390.66805194805187,60.54545454545456 346.6709090909091,122.78787878787875 285.9061971830985,187.1830985915493 180.6876712328767,292.24657534246575 63.80705479452055,380.75342465753425\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"249.04787961696306\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"249.04787961696306\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"63.80705479452055,379.5068493150685 180.6876712328767,292.24657534246575 285.9061971830985,258.9577464788732 346.6709090909091,172.4242424242424 390.66805194805187,164.54545454545456 411.83697368421053,49.13157894736844\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 2%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 292 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"63.80705479452055\" cy=\"379.5068493150685\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 35%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"180.6876712328767\" cy=\"292.24657534246575\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 64%&amp;#10;It rained 34% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"285.9061971830985\" cy=\"258.9577464788732\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 58% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"346.6709090909091\" cy=\"172.4242424242424\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 60% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"390.66805194805187\" cy=\"164.54545454545456\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 91% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 152 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.83697368421053\" cy=\"49.13157894736844\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(37%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Chattogram the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.29) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-3.43).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'>-3.425</td><td class='num'>2.7%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>80%</td><td class='num'>0.050</td><td class='num'>11.4%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>210</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.123</td><td class='num'>19.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.291</td><td class='num'>12.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":22.3384,"lon":91.83168,"n":731,"n_cities":216,"name":"Chattogram","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.2,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0164041095890411,"n":292,"obs":0.00684931506849315,"sig":false},{"hi":0.51,"lo":0.2,"mean":0.34657534246575344,"n":73,"obs":0.2465753424657534,"sig":false},{"hi":0.75,"lo":0.51,"mean":0.6438028169014083,"n":71,"obs":0.3380281690140845,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.75,"mean":0.8154545454545454,"n":66,"obs":0.5757575757575758,"sig":true},{"hi":0.99,"lo":0.9,"mean":0.9397402597402595,"n":77,"obs":0.5974025974025974,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.99,"mean":0.9995394736842106,"n":152,"obs":0.9144736842105263,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":7.7,"provisional":false,"rank":45,"rank_hi":103.02499999999998,"rank_lo":15.975000000000001,"reliability":0.02915315045152899,"resolution":0.12518920450889692,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"chattogram","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Dhaka"}